"""Source-reviewed 2023 STANDATA interpretations and bulletins."""
import pathlib,json,re
out=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
notes=json.loads((out/'reviewed-notes.json').read_text());records=json.loads((out/'index.json').read_text())
def put(codes,summary,scope,conditions,cites,topics):
 for r in records:
  if any(r['id'].endswith('-'+c) for c in codes.split()):
   notes[r['id']]=dict(summary=summary,applies_to=scope,conditions=conditions.split('|'),selected_citations=cites.split(),topics=topics.split(),conditions_completeness='Source navigation summary; read the full interpretation/bulletin and any referenced standards before applying it.')
 (out/'reviewed-notes.json').write_text(json.dumps(notes,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
put('23-bci-001','Explains building/fire-code treatment of storage sea-cans and why normal prefabricated steel-building certifications do not automatically cover them.','Shipping containers for material storage with authorized-personnel access.','Determine the applicable building and fire requirements and identify dangerous-goods storage in the fire safety plan.|Do not assume CSA A660 or A277 certification applies to shipping containers.','A:1.4.1.2. B:4.1.1.1.','occupancy-and-accessibility structural-and-framing evidence-and-conformity')
put('23-bci-002','Distinguishes residential dayhomes from daycare occupancies offering overnight care and consolidates their safety requirements.','Licensed overnight child-care dayhomes/daycares.','Establish the occupancy classification before selecting protections.|Address the specified smoke/CO detection, sleeping-room escape, fire alarm/sprinkler and emergency-planning measures for that category.','A:1.4.1.2. B:3.2.4.20. B:9.10.19.2.','occupancy-and-accessibility housing-secondary-suites-part9 firefighting-alarms-sprinklers')
put('23-bci-003 23-bci-003r1','Coordinates design and operational occupant-load calculations for assembly uses.','Assembly occupancies/licensed beverage establishments under building and fire authorities.','Use the lowest applicable limit from the listed alarm, sprinkler, egress and occupant-density criteria.|Coordinate both AHJs; this document is an interpretation rather than a variance increasing capacity.','B:3.1.17.1. B:3.4.2.6. B:3.2.5.12.','occupancy-and-accessibility egress-and-single-stair firefighting-alarms-sprinklers')
put('23-bci-004','Clarifies permits and the use of NFPA 33 for spray-finishing systems where the building code relies on good engineering practice.','Spray booths, areas and rooms involving flammable/combustible materials.','Apply NFPA 33 for the relevant systems.|Obtain building, electrical and gas permits as applicable.','B:6.9.1.2. B:6.2.1.1.','hvac-ventilation-plumbing professional-involvement process-and-admin')
for code,org in [('23-bci-005','QAI Laboratories'),('23-bci-006','ULC/UL Solutions'),('23-bci-007','Intertek'),('23-bci-013','ICC Evaluation Service'),('23-bci-040','APA – The Engineered Wood Association')]:
 put(code,f'Recognizes {org} as an approved organization issuing product evaluation reports for use in Alberta.','Evaluation reports within the organization’s recognized/accredited scope.','Maintain Standards Council of Canada accreditation.|Notify the Provincial Building Administrator of accreditation changes/lapse.|A report still has product-specific scope, limitations and edition requirements.','A:1.2.2.1.','evidence-and-conformity')
put('23-bci-008','Clarifies whether damper-operating smoke detectors must connect to a building fire alarm system.','Smoke/fire-smoke dampers in HVAC systems.','Detector operation does not by itself create a requirement for a building fire alarm system.|Where a fire alarm system is required, apply the identified detector/system installation, verification and signal requirements.','B:3.1.8.11.(3) B:3.2.4.1.','firefighting-alarms-sprinklers hvac-ventilation-plumbing fire-separations-and-spatial-separation')
put('23-bci-009','Separates installation/design authority from ongoing fire-code maintenance duties for commercial cooking suppression/exhaust systems.','Commercial kitchen fixed suppression and exhaust systems.','Consult the building AHJ on installation permits/professional involvement and the fire AHJ on ongoing testing/cleaning/maintenance.|Use the specified qualified people and referenced installation/maintenance standards.','B:6.3.1.6. B:9.10.1.4.','hvac-ventilation-plumbing firefighting-alarms-sprinklers professional-involvement')
put('23-bci-010','Explains multi-discipline safety-code permitting and emergency planning for special events.','Indoor/outdoor events requiring permits, occupant-load assessment or emergency planning.','Coordinate local AHJ and other relevant authorities.|Apply the relevant assembly, temporary-structure, occupancy, fire-protection and operational requirements.','B:3.1.17.1. B:3.1.18.1. C:2.2.11.1.','process-and-admin occupancy-and-accessibility egress-and-single-stair')
put('23-bci-011','Explains maintenance, replacement, modernization and alternative-solution options for existing fire alarm systems.','Existing fire alarm systems of any age undergoing work or testing.','Use people qualified for the activity; wiring repairs/replacement require qualified electricians.|Distinguish like-for-like replacement from a change of use or modernization.|Where current-code upgrading is not the chosen route, obtain the required documented alternative solution and supporting professional work.','A:1.1.1.2. B:3.2.4.5. B:3.2.4.19.','firefighting-alarms-sprinklers professional-involvement evidence-and-conformity')
put('23-bci-012 23-bci-012-rev1 23-bci-012r2','Clarifies professional authentication boundaries for individual services in five-or-more-unit rowhousing.','Residential rowhouses with no dwelling above/below another and at least five dwelling units.','Individual-unit electrical/water/drainage/gas/HVAC systems receive the stated limited treatment at the listed service boundaries.|Shared/common systems and other professional design obligations remain subject to the source and code.|Use the latest R2 multi-discipline interpretation rather than superseded versions.','C:2.4.1.1.','professional-involvement housing-secondary-suites-part9 hvac-ventilation-plumbing')
put('23-bci-014','Defines the professional qualifications of an integrated testing coordinator for fire/life-safety systems.','Integrated testing of fire-protection/life-safety systems and interacting building systems.','Coordinator must be a registered engineering professional knowledgeable and experienced in system design, installation and operation.','C:2.4.1.4. B:3.2.9.1. B:9.10.1.2.','professional-involvement firefighting-alarms-sprinklers')
put('23-bci-015 23-bci-015r1','Requires engineered/authenticated wood trusses and their connections as an assembly, including necessary interface information.','Wood trusses and roof assemblies in Part 9 buildings.','Have the registered engineer design and authenticate the required truss/connection information.|Information need not be duplicated on separately authenticated drawings where already covered.|Give authenticated documents to the AHJ before the specified inspection/covering approval; check the implementation date in the source.','B:9.23.14.11. C:2.4.1.2.','professional-involvement structural-and-framing')
put('23-bci-016 23-bci-016r1','Distinguishes AHJ assessment of code-exempt accessibility situations from a provincial barrier-free relaxation request.','Projects assessed for the listed barrier-free exceptions/uses.','AHJ/SCO must establish that an exemption or partial exemption applies.|Otherwise use the proper provincial relaxation process; this is not an applicant-selected universal exemption.','B:3.8.2.1.(1) C:2.2.1.4.','occupancy-and-accessibility process-and-admin')
put('23-bci-017','Explains when charging lights for listed photoluminescent exit signs need not connect to emergency power.','Photoluminescent exit signs and their dedicated charging lights.','Keep normal-power charging illumination continuous and on a dedicated circuit.|Restrict controls to authorized personnel and meet listing light-type/lux conditions.|Follow manufacturer installation instructions and listed/tested duration labelling.','B:3.4.5.1.(5) B:9.9.11.3.(5)','egress-and-single-stair evidence-and-conformity')
put('23-bci-018','Discusses fall/collision protection for low glazing and openable windows; the official publication is on hold under review.','Window glazing positioned where guard/fall-protection concerns arise.','ON HOLD – UNDER REVIEW: do not treat the interpretation as currently available permission.|Refer directly to current code and the AHJ for fixed/openable glazing and fall/collision protection.','B:9.8.8.1. B:3.3.1.18.','occupancy-and-accessibility housing-secondary-suites-part9 evidence-and-conformity')
put('23-bci-019','Distinguishes care occupancy from ordinary residential occupancy based on the services actually intended/provided.','Supportive-living accommodations without treatment services.','Owner must identify the intended use/services.|Use B3 where care services fall within that classification and C where those care services are absent.','A:1.4.1.2.','occupancy-and-accessibility')
put('23-bci-020','Clarifies appliance categories and when combustion systems need protection against dwelling depressurization.','Fuel-fired space/water-heating appliances and dwelling ventilation.','Categories I/II are not treated as mechanically vented or direct-vented for this purpose.|Categories III/IV and qualifying fully enclosed direct-vent arrangements receive the stated treatment.|Identify the actual appliance category/venting configuration before applying the protection rule.','B:9.32.3.8.','hvac-ventilation-plumbing housing-secondary-suites-part9')
put('23-bci-021','Explains current Part 10 relocatable industrial accommodation certification and renovation labelling.','New units built on/after May 1, 2024 and renovations to existing certified units.','New units require the appropriate CSA A277 label/specification sheet.|In-situ renovations require permits and applicable Municipal Affairs green labels applied through AHJ inspection.|Follow the source’s separate factory-renovation process.','C:2.5.1.1.','process-and-admin evidence-and-conformity')
put('23-bci-022','Identifies certain building uses that may be exempt from the building energy-efficiency provisions.','Listed low-occupancy industrial/equipment shelters and specific impractical-to-comply uses.','Establish the actual occupancy and use; exclusion is not inferred from an industrial label alone.|Refer irregular/unique cases to the AHJ.|Moisture/comfort insulation obligations are a separate consideration.','B:9.36.1.3. B:9.25.2.1.','energy-efficiency occupancy-and-accessibility')
put('23-bci-023','Clarifies the building-envelope definition as it applies to attic/roof-space separation and ventilation.','Residential buildings with one or more dwelling units.','Include assemblies separating the attic/roof space from outside/ground, its ventilation, and separation from conditioned space.|Use this interpretation to identify the relevant envelope rather than to waive assembly performance.','A:1.4.1.2.','building-envelope-insulation-cladding')
put('23-bci-024','Explains the application/review route for demonstrating that an F1 industrial hazard has been reduced to an F2-equivalent risk.','Buildings/parts classified as F1 industrial occupancy.','Use a qualified Alberta registered engineer’s hazard/performance analysis.|Submit the required alternative-solution documentation, including operating/maintenance limitations.|AHJ acceptance and enforcement remain necessary; this interpretation is not a generic reclassification approval.','C:2.3.1.1. C:2.3.1.2. A:1.2.1.1.','occupancy-and-accessibility professional-involvement process-and-admin evidence-and-conformity')
put('23-bci-025','Assigns building-SCO review of energy-storage-system room construction and clarifies dual permit needs.','Service/utility rooms required by the identified electrical-code ESS rules.','Obtain an electrical permit for the installation and a building permit for required room construction.|Building SCO reviews/inspects the room construction against the stated requirements.','B:9.10.3.1.','fire-separations-and-spatial-separation process-and-admin')
put('23-bci-026','Confirms that single-egress-stair residential designs can follow the alternative-solution route when acceptable solutions call for multiple stairs.','Residential buildings proposing fewer stairs than the prescriptive acceptable solution.','Submit a Division C alternative-solution case demonstrating the required performance against attributed objectives/functions.|Keep issued variance documentation available on the premises and maintain ongoing compliance.|This is an application pathway, not a blanket approval of a single-stair design.','A:1.2.1.1.(1) C:2.3.1.1. C:2.3.1.2.','egress-and-single-stair professional-involvement evidence-and-conformity process-and-admin')
put('23-bci-030','Consolidates building/fire-code considerations for reducing fire spread during construction/demolition.','Construction/demolition sites from houses to multistorey buildings.','Coordinate a risk assessment and protection measures with the AHJ/SCO.|Account for adjacent exposure, available firefighting capacity, water/access and fire safety planning.|The suggestions are not an exhaustive prescriptive design.','B:8.1.1.1. B:3.2.5.6.','fire-separations-and-spatial-separation firefighting-alarms-sprinklers process-and-admin')
put('23-bci-032','Clarifies industrial classification and safeguards for buildings used to park/repair/service tank vehicles.','Tank-vehicle buildings where flammable/combustible contents or vapours may be present.','Identify actual parking/repair/service activities and hazardous contents.|Apply the stated F1 design, ventilation, electrical-area and ignition-source controls where required.','A:1.4.1.2.','occupancy-and-accessibility hvac-ventilation-plumbing firefighting-alarms-sprinklers')
put('23-bci-034','Clarifies the duty to maintain operational elevating devices serving a required accessible path in residential buildings.','Residential buildings whose required barrier-free path is served by an elevator/platform device.','Maintain the device in service or provide accepted equivalent accessibility measures.|Necessary repairs/emergency shutdowns require reasonable and diligent handling under the source.|SCO enforcement does not make every temporary repair outage a permanent exemption.','B:3.8.2.3. B:3.8.3.7.','occupancy-and-accessibility process-and-admin')
put('23-bci-035','Explains the garage-separation exception where an attached garage serves a house with a secondary suite.','Attached storage garages for five vehicles or fewer serving that house/suite arrangement.','Apply the exception only to the garage serving the dwelling/house to which it is attached or in which it is built.|Check the remaining garage and secondary-suite separation requirements.','B:9.10.9.18.(3)','housing-secondary-suites-part9 fire-separations-and-spatial-separation')
put('23-bci-037','Clarifies the applicable lightning-protection standard and electrical permitting.','New/altered/added lightning-protection systems.','Comply with CAN/CSA-B72:20.|An electrical permit is required; this work alone does not require a building permit under this interpretation.','B:3.6.1.3.','process-and-admin evidence-and-conformity')
put('23-bci-038','Clarifies whether alterations to existing elevators require firefighters’ emergency-operation upgrades.','Existing elevating devices where FEO was not originally installed/required.','Registered professional must verify the code/requirements at initial installation during the permit process.|Apply the actual alteration provisions; a controller capable of FEO is not alone an installed FEO system.|Separate requirements apply when an existing FEO system is altered.','B:3.5.2.1. B:3.2.4.14.','occupancy-and-accessibility firefighting-alarms-sprinklers professional-involvement')
put('23-bci-042','Explains design/submission and verification for hydronic systems heating building interiors.','Primary/secondary interior hydronic heat; excludes systems such as exterior snowmelt that do not heat the building interior.','Submit the specified professionally prepared generic package plus project-specific design data/plans.|Use a qualified designer under the stated alternatives and obtain the required system verification/documentation.','B:9.33.4.1.(1) C:2.4.1.1.(3)','hvac-ventilation-plumbing professional-involvement evidence-and-conformity')
put('23-bci-043','Coordinates permits, professional involvement and qualified installation/testing of electromagnetic locks connected to fire alarms.','New/existing maglock installations and their maintenance/testing/verification.','Obtain applicable permits for new work/modifications.|Retain registered engineering involvement when size, occupancy or complexity requires it.|Use qualified persons and complete the required fire-alarm/interface verification and ongoing testing.','C:2.4.1.1. B:3.2.9.1. B:3.2.4.5.','egress-and-single-stair firefighting-alarms-sprinklers professional-involvement')
put('23-bcb-001','Explains Alberta’s Tier 1 housing energy requirements and distinguishes voluntary higher tiers.','Housing/small-building energy compliance under Section 9.36.','Use the adopted Tier 1 provisions; do not automatically import every higher-tier requirement.|Check the stated airtightness/modelling treatment and voluntary-tier conditions.','B:9.36.1.3. B:9.36.7.3. B:9.36.5.10.','energy-efficiency')
put('23-bcb-002 23-bcb-002r1','Historical roof-truss documentation bulletin for one- and two-family dwellings; now archived.','Former truss submission/authentication arrangements.','Do not use the archived bulletin to override 23-BCI-015R1.|For present submissions check the current interpretation and municipal implementation requirements.','B:9.23.14.11. C:2.4.1.1. C:2.4.1.2.','structural-and-framing professional-involvement')
put('23-bcb-003','Archived joint electrical variance/building bulletin addressing residential energy-storage installations before adoption of the newer electrical code.','Historical residential ESS installations under the 2021 electrical code.','The source limits single ESS capacity and specifies location, enclosure, listing and permit controls.|The source says its temporary variance ceases when the 2024 electrical code is adopted.|This is not a current NBC building variance.','B:9.10.3.1.','fire-separations-and-spatial-separation process-and-admin evidence-and-conformity')
put('23-bcb-004','Provides guidance for AHJ permission to occupy completed parts of buildings while construction continues.','Phased occupancy, occupied additions and alterations.','Obtain AHJ permission/occupancy permit.|Coordinate a construction fire safety plan, required systems and safe separation of occupied/work areas.','C:2.2.11.1.(1) B:8.1.1.1.(3)','process-and-admin firefighting-alarms-sprinklers fire-separations-and-spatial-separation')
put('23-bcb-005','Explains acceptance and limitations of listed/certified sprinkler antifreeze solutions.','Existing/new sprinkler systems designed with antifreeze.','Use a listed/certified solution and check listing compatibility, temperature, volume/pressure and maintenance limitations.|Do not assume a solution accepted for one system is compatible with another.','','firefighting-alarms-sprinklers evidence-and-conformity')
put('23-bcb-006','Explains SEER2/HSPF2 equipment-efficiency metrics and their relationship to code requirements.','Electrically operated air-cooled air conditioners and heat pumps under NBC(AE)/NECB.','Check applicable equipment-efficiency rules and the stated test/metric conversion context.|Do not treat a changed rating label as a standalone performance equivalence finding.','B:9.36.3.10.','energy-efficiency hvac-ventilation-plumbing evidence-and-conformity')
put('23-bcb-007 23-bcb-007r1','Consolidates dispersed Part 9 secondary-suite provisions for navigation alongside the actual code.','Houses with a secondary suite.','Use the latest R1 version.|Check every applicable code provision directly; this compilation is not a complete design guide or issued alternative solution.','A:1.4.1.2. B:9.10.11.2. B:9.10.9.3. B:9.32.1.2.','housing-secondary-suites-part9 fire-separations-and-spatial-separation hvac-ventilation-plumbing')
